{"content":[{"id":"c66060e","settings":{"flex_direction":"column"},"elements":[{"id":"3e9e3630","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">When your HVAC system starts making a strange noise, it\u2019s hard to know if it\u2019s a minor annoyance or the first sign of a serious problem. From a rattling outdoor unit in Louisburg to a buzzing heat pump in Raleigh or Wake Forest, homeowners across Central and Eastern North Carolina deal with these sounds every season as temperatures and humidity swing.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/dolandesignhvac.com\/\"><b>Dolan Design Heating &amp; Cooling<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, we\u2019ve spent more than 25 years helping families in Louisburg, Raleigh, Wake Forest, Zebulon, Youngsville, and nearby areas track down HVAC noises before they turn into breakdowns, comfort issues, or expensive repairs.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Use this guide to understand what those sounds usually mean, what you can safely check yourself, and when it\u2019s time to call in a Dolan Design technician.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"},{"id":"4856f5f5","settings":{"flex_direction":"column"},"elements":[{"id":"3be4a563","settings":{"html":"<div style=\"border: 2px solid #305ca6; border-radius: 12px; background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 20px; max-width: 1200px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: #1a1a1a;\">\r\n<h3 style=\"background-color: #305ca6; color: #ffffff; padding: 12px 15px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 0 0 15px 0; font-size: 20px;\">\r\nQuick Guide: What Common HVAC Noises Usually Mean in NC Homes\r\n<\/h3>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 15px; color: #333333;\">\r\nIf you just want the fast overview, start here:\r\n<\/p>\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 0;\">\r\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n<strong style=\"color: #f16022;\">Banging<\/strong> \u2013 Often tied to ignition issues, blower problems, or expanding ductwork\r\n<\/li>\r\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n<strong style=\"color: #f16022;\">Rattling<\/strong> \u2013 Loose panels, hardware, or debris in or around the unit\r\n<\/li>\r\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n<strong style=\"color: #f16022;\">Buzzing<\/strong> \u2013 Electrical strain, a struggling motor, debris near the fan, or refrigerant issues\r\n<\/li>\r\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n<strong style=\"color: #f16022;\">Hissing<\/strong> \u2013 Air escaping from duct leaks or a possible refrigerant leak\r\n<\/li>\r\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">\r\n<strong style=\"color: #f16022;\">Whistling<\/strong> \u2013 Blocked airflow from dirty filters, closed vents, or undersized ductwork\r\n<\/li>\r\n<\/ul>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top: 15px; font-weight: bold; color: #1a1a1a;\">\r\nIf the noise is new, louder than normal, or doesn\u2019t go away, it\u2019s time to schedule a professional HVAC inspection.\r\n<\/p>\r\n<\/div>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"html","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"},{"id":"2e93271b","settings":{"flex_direction":"column"},"elements":[{"id":"1924f6a3","settings":{"title":"1. Rattling \u2014 Loose Hardware or Debris\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"8de9c33","settings":{"title":"What it sounds like\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"70ea4e08","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A light clatter, shake, or vibration that\u2019s more noticeable during startup or when the fan ramps up.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"cac7694","settings":{"title":"What\u2019s usually causing it\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"73619f23","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rattling is often your system\u2019s way of telling you something is loose, worn, or bouncing around. In North Carolina, outdoor units are magnets for pine needles, acorns, leaves, and mulch.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Common causes include:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Loose cabinet screws or panels<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">An air handler or furnace door that isn\u2019t fully latched<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Worn or unbalanced fan blades<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Debris inside or around the outdoor unit<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"656cef05","settings":{"title":"What you can safely check yourself","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"7aca799","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You don\u2019t need tools or HVAC knowledge to do a <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/www.angi.com\/articles\/hvac-inspection-checklist.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">basic check<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Make sure nothing is leaning against or touching the outdoor unit<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Gently press on metal panels to see if one is loose or vibrating<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Check that the air handler or furnace door is firmly latched<\/span><\/li><\/ul><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the rattling keeps coming back, something inside is likely wearing out or working loose.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"73e3f89","settings":{"title":"When to call Dolan Design\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"378ab206","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Persistent rattling can lead to:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Blower wheel imbalance<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Motor damage<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cracked or fatigued metal housings<\/span><\/li><\/ul><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the noise doesn\u2019t resolve quickly after your basic checks, <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/dolandesignhvac.com\/contact\/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">schedule a diagnostic visit<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> with Dolan Design so we can catch the issue before it becomes a bigger repair.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"54238e5d","settings":{"title":"2. Banging \u2014 Ignition or Blower Problems\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"145941c5","settings":{"title":"What it sounds like","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6dd1f387","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A loud bang, boom, or heavy thump \u2014 often right when the system starts up.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1b438826","settings":{"title":"What it often means\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"43277a37","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Banging is one of the more serious HVAC noises, especially in older systems or equipment that hasn\u2019t been maintained regularly.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Possible causes:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Delayed ignition<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> \u2013 Gas or fuel builds up, then ignites all at once<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Loose blower components<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> \u2013 The blower wheel or housing tapping or slamming as it starts<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Expanding or contracting <\/b><a href=\"https:\/\/www.trane.com\/residential\/en\/resources\/glossary\/ductwork\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><b>ductwork<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> \u2013 Metal popping or banging as it heats and cools (less urgent, but worth checking)<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"7dc5f23e","settings":{"title":"What you can safely check yourself","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"fd4fd21","settings":{"editor":"<ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Replace your air filter if it\u2019s dirty or overdue<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pay attention to <\/span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">when<\/span><\/i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> the bang happens (startup, shutdown, random)<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Make note of any other symptoms: weak airflow, odd smells, or frequent cycling<\/span><\/li><\/ul><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Share that timing and detail with<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/dolandesignhvac.com\/230688-2\/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> your technician<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> \u2014 it helps narrow the cause faster.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"7256351b","settings":{"title":"When to call Dolan Design\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"63bbef05","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the banging repeats, <\/span><b>turn the system off and call for service.<\/b><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Delayed ignition can damage the heat exchanger, creating a serious <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/dolandesignhvac.com\/essential-heating-inspection-detecting-carbon-monoxide\/\" data-wplink-edit=\"true\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">carbon monoxide risk<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"4aa7e83f","settings":{"title":"3. Buzzing \u2014 Electrical Issues or Outdoor Unit Strain"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"52b52565","settings":{"title":"What it sounds like\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"730ad4ba","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A steady hum, buzz, or vibrating sound from the outdoor unit or from the indoor cabinet. It may be constant or mostly when the system is starting or under heavy load.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"225a76e1","settings":{"title":"What it usually means","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"7f864bac","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Buzzing often points to electrical or mechanical strain \u2014 a component working harder than it should, or starting to fail.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Frequent sources include:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Loose or failing electrical contacts or relays<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A motor under heavy strain or nearing the end of its life<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Debris around the outdoor fan (twigs, leaves, plastic, etc.)<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Low refrigerant pressure putting stress on the compressor<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">An outdoor unit that has shifted or sunk, causing vibration<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5eb33048","settings":{"title":"What you can safely check\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5112131d","settings":{"editor":"<ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Look through the top or side grill of the outdoor unit for visible debris<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Make sure the outdoor unit is reasonably level and not sitting in a sinkhole or mud<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Notice when the buzzing happens: only on startup, only outdoors, or constantly<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"7a16c9d6","settings":{"title":"When to call Dolan Design\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3b9537e0","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If buzzing:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Keeps getting louder<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Comes with <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/dolandesignhvac.com\/winter-hvac-upgrades-louisburg-nc\/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">weak heating or cooling<\/span><\/a><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Is paired with tripped breakers or burning smells<\/span><\/li><\/ul><p><a href=\"https:\/\/dolandesignhvac.com\/contact\/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u2026you need a professional to inspect it<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Electrical issues escalate quickly and can damage major components if left alone.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5f96c9e9","settings":{"title":"4. Hissing \u2014 Air Leaks or Refrigerant Pressure\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"49fef201","settings":{"title":"What it sounds like","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"608593da","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A light or sharp hiss from vents, ducts, refrigerant lines, or the outdoor unit. It might be constant or only when the system is running.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3d9bb7fa","settings":{"title":"What it often means","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1e0e854","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hissing almost always means something is escaping under pressure.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Typical causes:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Leaky or poorly sealed duct joints<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Air bypassing a filter that isn\u2019t seated correctly<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Refrigerant escaping from copper lines, coils, or valves<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"551ac27f","settings":{"title":"What you can check yourself","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"7765fa28","settings":{"editor":"<ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Make sure vents and return grilles aren\u2019t blocked by furniture, rugs, or baskets<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you can safely access them, look for obviously separated or damaged duct joints<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Listen for whether the hissing stops when the system shuts off<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5c8b837f","settings":{"title":"When to call Dolan Design\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"4490571f","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Call right away if the hissing:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Comes from copper lines, the outdoor unit, or near the indoor coil<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Continues briefly after the system shuts off<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Shows up along with poor cooling or ice on lines\/coils<\/span><\/li><\/ul><p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.homedepot.com\/c\/ah\/how-to-fix-ac-freon-leaks\/9ba683603be9fa5395fab901fe1b613a\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Refrigerant leaks<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> don\u2019t fix themselves. Running a system low on refrigerant can destroy the compressor \u2014 one of the most expensive parts in your HVAC system.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"2b8c5407","settings":{"title":"5. Whistling \u2014 Airflow Restrictions or Duct Issues\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"64c4b99f","settings":{"title":"What it sounds like\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"46e0923f","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A high-pitched whistle, whoosh, or squeal from vents, returns, or door gaps.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"22ef40f","settings":{"title":"What it usually means","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5f725e33","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Whistling is almost always an airflow problem. The system is trying to pull or push more air than the ducts or openings easily allow.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Common causes include:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Dirty or clogged air filters<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Partially closed supply vents<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Return grilles blocked by furniture or d\u00e9cor<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Undersized, aging, or poorly designed ductwork<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3dce2734","settings":{"title":"What you can check yourself","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"40880299","settings":{"editor":"<ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Replace the air filter if you can\u2019t remember the last time you changed it<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Open all supply vents fully (closing vents to <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/www.homesandgardens.com\/solved\/should-you-close-vents-in-unused-rooms\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u201csave energy\u201d<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> usually backfires)<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Clear returns of furniture, baskets, curtains, or decor<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6d2b7837","settings":{"title":"When to call Dolan Design\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"5a9bb66","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If whistling continues even after you\u2019ve opened vents and changed filters, the issue may involve:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ducts that are too small or restrictive<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Blower settings that don\u2019t match your duct design<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Older, pieced-together ductwork that needs redesign or replacement<\/span><\/li><\/ul><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Dolan Design can evaluate your system\u2019s airflow and static pressure to <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/dolandesignhvac.com\/contact\/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">find the root cause and recommend the right fix.<\/span><\/a><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"35b63806","settings":{"title":"HVAC Noise FAQs for Louisburg & Raleigh Area Homeowners"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"76670109","settings":{"html":"<style>\r\n.dd-accordion {\r\n  max-width: 800px;\r\n  margin: 0 auto 30px;\r\n  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.dd-accordion-item {\r\n  border: 1px solid #305ca6;\r\n  border-radius: 8px;\r\n  margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n  overflow: hidden;\r\n  background-color: #f3f4f6;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.dd-accordion-header {\r\n  margin: 0;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.dd-accordion-button {\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  text-align: left;\r\n  padding: 14px 16px;\r\n  font-size: 16px;\r\n  font-weight: 600;\r\n  border: none;\r\n  background-color: #305ca6;\r\n  color: #ffffff;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n  display: flex;\r\n  justify-content: space-between;\r\n  align-items: center;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.dd-accordion-button:focus {\r\n  outline: 2px solid #f16022;\r\n  outline-offset: 2px;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.dd-accordion-icon {\r\n  margin-left: 12px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.dd-accordion-panel {\r\n  max-height: 0;\r\n  overflow: hidden;\r\n  transition: max-height 0.25s ease-out;\r\n  background-color: #f3f4f6;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.dd-accordion-panel-inner {\r\n  padding: 12px 16px 16px;\r\n  color: #1a1a1a;\r\n  font-size: 15px;\r\n  line-height: 1.5;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.dd-accordion-panel p {\r\n  margin: 0 0 8px;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.dd-accordion-panel ul {\r\n  margin: 0 0 8px 20px;\r\n  padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.dd-accordion-panel li {\r\n  margin-bottom: 4px;\r\n}\r\n\r\n.dd-accordion-button.active {\r\n  background-color: #f16022;\r\n}\r\n<\/style>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"dd-accordion\" id=\"hvac-noise-faq-accordion\">\r\n\r\n  <!-- Item 1 -->\r\n  <div class=\"dd-accordion-item\">\r\n    <h3 class=\"dd-accordion-header\">\r\n      <button class=\"dd-accordion-button\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\r\n        <span>Are some HVAC noises normal?<\/span>\r\n        <span class=\"dd-accordion-icon\">+<\/span>\r\n      <\/button>\r\n    <\/h3>\r\n    <div class=\"dd-accordion-panel\">\r\n      <div class=\"dd-accordion-panel-inner\">\r\n        <p>Yes. A low hum and gentle fan noise are normal. Sudden, sharp, grinding, banging, or brand-new noises should always be checked.<\/p>\r\n      <\/div>\r\n    <\/div>\r\n  <\/div>\r\n\r\n  <!-- Item 2 -->\r\n  <div class=\"dd-accordion-item\">\r\n    <h3 class=\"dd-accordion-header\">\r\n      <button class=\"dd-accordion-button\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\r\n        <span>Why would my HVAC suddenly start making noise?<\/span>\r\n        <span class=\"dd-accordion-icon\">+<\/span>\r\n      <\/button>\r\n    <\/h3>\r\n    <div class=\"dd-accordion-panel\">\r\n      <div class=\"dd-accordion-panel-inner\">\r\n        <p>Weather swings, worn parts, loose hardware, debris in the outdoor unit, or changes in airflow (closed vents, dirty filters, new furniture placement) can all create new sounds almost overnight.<\/p>\r\n      <\/div>\r\n    <\/div>\r\n  <\/div>\r\n\r\n  <!-- Item 3 -->\r\n  <div class=\"dd-accordion-item\">\r\n    <h3 class=\"dd-accordion-header\">\r\n      <button class=\"dd-accordion-button\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\r\n        <span>Is it safe to keep running a noisy system?<\/span>\r\n        <span class=\"dd-accordion-icon\">+<\/span>\r\n      <\/button>\r\n    <\/h3>\r\n    <div class=\"dd-accordion-panel\">\r\n      <div class=\"dd-accordion-panel-inner\">\r\n        <p>Light, short-lived noise might be safe for a short time \u2014 but don\u2019t ignore anything that\u2019s new, worsening, or accompanied by strange smells, weak airflow, or frequent cycling.<\/p>\r\n        <p>If the noise is loud, metallic, or comes with burning or gas smells, turn the system off and call for service.<\/p>\r\n      <\/div>\r\n    <\/div>\r\n  <\/div>\r\n\r\n  <!-- Item 4 -->\r\n  <div class=\"dd-accordion-item\">\r\n    <h3 class=\"dd-accordion-header\">\r\n      <button class=\"dd-accordion-button\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\r\n        <span>Can ductwork be the reason my system is so loud?<\/span>\r\n        <span class=\"dd-accordion-icon\">+<\/span>\r\n      <\/button>\r\n    <\/h3>\r\n    <div class=\"dd-accordion-panel\">\r\n      <div class=\"dd-accordion-panel-inner\">\r\n        <p>Definitely. Loose joints, undersized duct runs, sharp turns, and pressure imbalances are common noise sources in homes around Louisburg, Raleigh, Wake Forest, and Zebulon.<\/p>\r\n        <p>Sometimes fixing the ductwork makes just as much difference as working on the equipment.<\/p>\r\n      <\/div>\r\n    <\/div>\r\n  <\/div>\r\n\r\n  <!-- Item 5 -->\r\n  <div class=\"dd-accordion-item\">\r\n    <h3 class=\"dd-accordion-header\">\r\n      <button class=\"dd-accordion-button\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\r\n        <span>How do I reduce HVAC noise long-term?<\/span>\r\n        <span class=\"dd-accordion-icon\">+<\/span>\r\n      <\/button>\r\n    <\/h3>\r\n    <div class=\"dd-accordion-panel\">\r\n      <div class=\"dd-accordion-panel-inner\">\r\n        <ul>\r\n          <li>Change air filters regularly<\/li>\r\n          <li>Keep vents fully open and returns clear<\/li>\r\n          <li>Schedule seasonal maintenance and tune-ups<\/li>\r\n          <li>Address minor noises before they become big repairs<\/li>\r\n          <li>Ask about ductwork improvements if you have persistent hot\/cold spots<\/li>\r\n        <\/ul>\r\n      <\/div>\r\n    <\/div>\r\n  <\/div>\r\n\r\n  <!-- Item 6 -->\r\n  <div class=\"dd-accordion-item\">\r\n    <h3 class=\"dd-accordion-header\">\r\n      <button class=\"dd-accordion-button\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\r\n        <span>Are HVAC noise problems more common in North Carolina\u2019s climate?<\/span>\r\n        <span class=\"dd-accordion-icon\">+<\/span>\r\n      <\/button>\r\n    <\/h3>\r\n    <div class=\"dd-accordion-panel\">\r\n      <div class=\"dd-accordion-panel-inner\">\r\n        <p>Yes. Our climate is hard on outdoor equipment and ductwork. Moisture, shifting soil, and debris can all speed up wear, especially on older systems and poorly maintained equipment.<\/p>\r\n      <\/div>\r\n    <\/div>\r\n  <\/div>\r\n\r\n<\/div>\r\n\r\n<script>\r\ndocument.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {\r\n  var accordion = document.getElementById('hvac-noise-faq-accordion');\r\n  if (!accordion) return;\r\n\r\n  var buttons = accordion.querySelectorAll('.dd-accordion-button');\r\n\r\n  buttons.forEach(function (btn) {\r\n    btn.addEventListener('click', function () {\r\n      var isActive = btn.classList.contains('active');\r\n      var panel = btn.parentElement.nextElementSibling;\r\n      var icon = btn.querySelector('.dd-accordion-icon');\r\n\r\n      \/\/ Close all items\r\n      buttons.forEach(function (otherBtn) {\r\n        otherBtn.classList.remove('active');\r\n        otherBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');\r\n        var otherPanel = otherBtn.parentElement.nextElementSibling;\r\n        var otherIcon = otherBtn.querySelector('.dd-accordion-icon');\r\n        otherPanel.style.maxHeight = null;\r\n        if (otherIcon) otherIcon.textContent = '+';\r\n      });\r\n\r\n      \/\/ Toggle current\r\n      if (!isActive) {\r\n        btn.classList.add('active');\r\n        btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');\r\n        panel.style.maxHeight = panel.scrollHeight + 'px';\r\n        if (icon) icon.textContent = '\u2013';\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n<\/script>\r\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"html","elType":"widget"},{"id":"be49392","settings":{"title":"Why NC Homeowners Choose Dolan Design Heating & Cooling\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1f6dcbd3","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Dolan Design Heating &amp; Cooling is a locally trusted HVAC and plumbing company based in Louisburg, NC, serving homeowners<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/dolandesignhvac.com\/service-areas\/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> across the Greater Raleigh area.<\/span><\/a><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Homeowners choose Dolan because we offer:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>30+ Years of Experience<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> serving Louisburg, Raleigh, Wake Forest, Youngsville, Zebulon &amp; beyond<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Better Air, Better Life Promise<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> focused on comfort, efficiency, and healthier homes<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><a href=\"https:\/\/dolandesignhvac.com\/contact\/\"><b>24\/7 Emergency Service<\/b> <\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u2014 real help when your system fails at the worst time<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Financing Available<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to make repairs and replacements more manageable<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><a href=\"https:\/\/dolandesignhvac.com\/hvac-services\/\"><b>Full-Service HVAC &amp; Plumbing<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> \u2013 heating, cooling, ductless, maintenance, and plumbing support<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Trusted Technicians<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> trained on all major brands and systems<\/span><\/li><\/ul><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Whether you\u2019re in Louisburg, Raleigh, Wake Forest, Zebulon, Youngsville, Wilson, Rocky Mount, Henderson, or Greenville, our team understands how North Carolina\u2019s climate affects your HVAC system and how to keep it running quietly and efficiently.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"624b4461","settings":{"title":"Schedule HVAC Noise Diagnostics with Dolan Design Heating & Cooling"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"4cc28e39","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If your HVAC system is making a strange noise, don\u2019t wait for it to become a no-heat emergency or a major repair bill.\u00a0<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A simple visit from Dolan Design can:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Identify what\u2019s causing the sound<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Prevent damage to expensive components<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Improve comfort and efficiency<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Help your system run quieter and last longer<\/span><\/li><\/ul><p><b>Call Dolan Design Heating &amp; Cooling at (919) 896-8630 or <\/b><a href=\"https:\/\/dolandesignhvac.com\/contact\/\"><b>request service online anytime<\/b> <\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">to schedule your HVAC noise diagnostic.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"}],"settings":{"template":"default"},"metadata":{"et_enqueued_post_fonts":"a:2:{s:6:\"family\";a:2:{s:10:\"et-gf-ruda\";s:32:\"Ruda:regular,500,600,700,800,900\";s:12:\"et-gf-ubuntu\";s:63:\"Ubuntu:300,300italic,regular,italic,500,500italic,700,700italic\";}s:6:\"subset\";a:2:{i:0;s:5:\"latin\";i:1;s:9:\"latin-ext\";}}"}}